invariant: INV-38
file: tls_write.c
catches: unit
reason: ch_writable_len does not count the KeyUpdate record ch_write sends
  first while an answer is owed, so it returns 27 bytes too many and a
  caller that sizes its output by it gets a write that does not fit.
  bin/unit holds what it returns to the real ch_write at every cap with
  an answer owed.

--- old
    size_t room = records_before_key_update(t);
--- new
    size_t room = t->key_update_owed ? SIZE_MAX : records_before_key_update(t);
